\fs24 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 short description: 
\f1\fs26 Architecture of Erosion is a series of vessels made from wild clay gathered in Bulgaria, as a way of getting closer to the place.
\f0 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\

\fs24 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 description: 
\f1\fs26 he clay for these vessels was collected from different places in Bulgaria. Gathering and working with the earth became a way of approaching a country through its material \'97 paying attention to where it comes from, how it feels, and what changes from one place to another. The vessels are built by hand and their surfaces are treated in different ways, leaving the material and the process visible. Their narrow bases give them a slightly precarious presence, always close to losing and finding their balance.
